Detailed analysis with code examples for 6-7 marks:

1. Linear Construct - O(n):
   - Pattern: Loop runs from 1 to n with a constant addition/subtraction step (`i++` or `i += c`).
   - Example Code:
     ```c
     int findMax(int arr[], int n) {
         int max = arr[0];
         for (int i = 1; i < n; i++) { // Executes n-1 times
             if (arr[i] > max) max = arr[i];
         }
         return max;
     }
     ```
   - Analysis: T(n) = c1 * n + c2 => O(n).

2. Quadratic Construct - O(n^2):
   - Pattern: Nested loops where an inner linear loop runs n times for every pass of the outer linear loop.
   - Example Code:
     ```c
     void bubbleSortPasses(int arr[], int n) {
         for (int i = 0; i < n - 1; i++) {         // Runs n-1 times
             for (int j = 0; j < n - i - 1; j++) { // Runs n-i-1 times
                 if (arr[j] > arr[j+1]) swap(&arr[j], &arr[j+1]);
             }
         }
     }
     ```
   - Analysis: Total operations = (n-1) + (n-2) + ... + 1 = n(n-1)/2 = 0.5n^2 - 0.5n => O(n^2).

3. Logarithmic Construct - O(log n):
   - Pattern: Loop variable changes exponentially by multiplication or division (`i *= 2` or `i /= 2`).
   - Example Code:
     ```c
     int binarySearch(int arr[], int n, int key) {
         int low = 0, high = n - 1;
         while (low <= high) { // Halves search space each step
             int mid = low + (high - low) / 2;
             if (arr[mid] == key) return mid;
             else if (arr[mid] < key) low = mid + 1;
             else high = mid - 1;
         }
         return -1;
     }
     ```
   - Analysis: Space halves at each step: n, n/2, n/4, ..., 1. Number of steps k satisfies n/2^k = 1 => k = log_2 n => O(log n).

